1
00:00:00,395 --> 00:00:04,679
Getting started. Set it up and give
it the one permission it needs.

2
00:00:05,945 --> 00:00:09,155
Open Gesture Volume.
The first time you open it,

3
00:00:09,195 --> 00:00:13,377
a short tour shows how the bar
works, one page at a time.

4
00:00:13,686 --> 00:00:18,071
Pick a style. Simple puts a round
button on the edge for volume.

5
00:00:18,111 --> 00:00:22,881
Advanced adds the Dock, the Quick slider,
the Deck and a long-press menu.

6
00:00:22,921 --> 00:00:24,632
You can switch any time.

7
00:00:24,973 --> 00:00:28,758
Learn the moves. The next
pages play each gesture out:

8
00:00:28,798 --> 00:00:32,908
swipe for volume, tap for the
volume panel, hold to move it.

9
00:00:33,573 --> 00:00:35,433
Allow the bar on screen.

10
00:00:35,473 --> 00:00:40,093
Tap Allow, switch on Allow display
over other apps, and come back.

11
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:43,490
That one switch lets the bar
sit on top of your apps.

12
00:00:44,173 --> 00:00:46,633
Notifications, if you like.

13
00:00:46,673 --> 00:00:50,433
Optional: allow notifications
and the bar’s controls wait

14
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:54,056
in your notification shade,
even with the app closed.

15
00:00:54,368 --> 00:00:58,603
Turn on the service. Tap Service
inactive to switch the bar on.

16
00:00:58,643 --> 00:01:02,337
Go home, and the round button
is waiting on the edge.

17
00:01:04,072 --> 00:01:06,624
Up next: Volume with a swipe.
